{"id":"mahabharata-3-213","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":213,"title":"त्रयोदशाधिकद्विशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 213 · Devasena and the desire of Agni","summary":{"en":"Markandeya begins the birth of Skanda. Indra rescues the maiden Devasena from the demon Keshin, and Brahma tells him that a mighty one born of Agni will be her husband and lead the gods' army; Agni, meanwhile, falls in love with the wives of the seven sages, and Svaha, who loves Agni, resolves to take their forms.","kn":"ಮಾರ್ಕಂಡೇಯರು ಸ್ಕಂದಜನ್ಮವನ್ನು ಆರಂಭಿಸುತ್ತಾರೆ. ಇಂದ್ರನು ದೇವಸೇನೆ ಎಂಬ ಕನ್ಯೆಯನ್ನು ಕೇಶಿ ದಾನವನಿಂದ ರಕ್ಷಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಅಗ್ನಿಯಿಂದ ಹುಟ್ಟುವ ಮಹಾಬಲನು ಅವಳ ಪತಿಯೂ ದೇವಸೇನಾಪತಿಯೂ ಆಗುವನೆಂದು ಬ್ರಹ್ಮ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಅತ್ತ ಅಗ್ನಿ ಸಪ್ತರ್ಷಿಪತ್ನಿಯರನ್ನು ಮೋಹಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ, ಅಗ್ನಿಯನ್ನು ಪ್ರೀತಿಸುವ ಸ್ವಾಹಾ ಅವರ ರೂಪ ಧರಿಸಲು ನಿಶ್ಚಯಿಸುತ್ತಾಳೆ.","hi":"मार्कण्डेय स्कन्द के जन्म की कथा आरम्भ करते हैं। इन्द्र कन्या देवसेना को दैत्य केशी से बचाते हैं, और ब्रह्मा बताते हैं कि अग्नि से जन्मा एक महाबली उसका पति और देवसेना का नायक होगा; इधर अग्नि सप्तर्षियों की पत्नियों पर मोहित होते हैं, और अग्नि से प्रेम करने वाली स्वाहा उनके रूप धरने का निश्चय करती हैं।","te":"మార్కండేయుడు స్కందుని జనన కథ ప్రారంభిస్తాడు. ఇంద్రుడు దేవసేన అనే కన్యను కేశి దానవుని నుండి రక్షిస్తాడు; అగ్ని నుండి పుట్టే మహాబలుడు ఆమె భర్త, దేవసేనాపతి అవుతాడని బ్రహ్మ చెబుతాడు; ఇంతలో అగ్ని సప్తర్షుల భార్యలను మోహిస్తాడు, అగ్నిని ప్రేమించే స్వాహా వారి రూపాలు ధరించాలని నిశ్చయిస్తుంది.","ta":"மார்க்கண்டேயர் ஸ்கந்தனின் பிறப்பைத் தொடங்குகிறார். இந்திரன் தேவஸேனை என்ற கன்னியைக் கேஶி அசுரனிடமிருந்து மீட்க, அக்னியிடமிருந்து பிறக்கும் வலியவன் அவள் கணவனும் தேவசேனைத் தலைவனுமாவான் என்று ப்ரஹ்மா சொல்கிறார்; இதற்கிடையில் அக்னி ஏழு முனிவர்களின் மனைவியர் மீது காதல் கொள்ள, அக்னியை நேசிக்கும் ஸ்வாஹா அவர்கள் உருவங்களை ஏற்கத் தீர்மானிக்கிறாள்.","ml":"സ്കന്ദന്റെ ജനനകഥ മാർക്കണ്ഡേയൻ ആരംഭിക്കുന്നു. കേശി എന്ന രാക്ഷസനിൽനിന്ന് ഇന്ദ്രൻ ദേവസേന എന്ന കന്യകയെ രക്ഷിക്കുന്നു; അഗ്നിയിൽനിന്ന് ജനിക്കുന്ന മഹാൻ അവളുടെ ഭർത്താവാകുകയും ദേവന്മാരുടെ സേനയെ നയിക്കുകയും ചെയ്യുമെന്ന് ബ്രഹ്മാവ് പറയുന്നു. അതിനിടെ അഗ്നി ഏഴു മുനിമാരുടെ പത്നിമാരിൽ മോഹിതനാകുന്നു; അഗ്നിയെ സ്നേഹിക്കുന്ന സ്വാഹാദേവി അവരുടെ രൂപം സ്വീകരിക്കാൻ തീരുമാനിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.213; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"मार्कण्डेयसमास्यापर्व","titleEn":"Markandeyasamasya Parva (Session with Markandeya)","verses":[{"text":"मार्कण्डेय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Markandeya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"अग्नीनां विविधो वंशः कीर्तितस्ते मयानघ ।\nशृणु जन्म तु कौरव्य कार्त्तिकेयस्य धीमतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Blameless one, I have told you the various lineages of the fires. Now hear, descendant of Kuru, the birth of the wise Karttikeya.\""}},{"n":2,"text":"अद्भुतस्याद्भुतं पुत्रं प्रवक्ष्याम्यमितौजसम् ।\nजातं सप्तर्षिभार्याभिर्ब्रह्मण्यं कीर्तिवर्धनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I will tell of the wondrous son of the Wondrous One, of immeasurable might, born through the wives of the seven sages, devoted to brahmins and a spreader of fame.\""}},{"n":3,"text":"देवासुराः पुरा यत्ता विनिघ्नन्तः परस्परम् ।\nतत्राजयन्सदा देवान्दानवा घोररूपिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Long ago the gods and asuras fought, striking one another; in that war the terrible-looking danavas kept defeating the gods.\""}},{"n":4,"text":"वध्यमानं बलं दृष्ट्वा बहुशस्तैः पुरंदरः ।\nस्वसैन्यनायकार्थाय चिन्तामाप भृशं तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Seeing his forces slain again and again by them, Indra (Purandara) then fell into deep worry about finding a commander for his army.\""}},{"n":5,"text":"देवसेनां दानवैर्यो भग्नां दृष्ट्वा महाबलः ।\nपालयेद्वीर्यमाश्रित्य स ज्ञेयः पुरुषो मया ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"He thought: 'The mighty man who, seeing the gods' army broken by the danavas, can protect it by his valor, is the one I must find.'\""}},{"n":6,"text":"स शैलं मानसं गत्वा ध्यायन्नर्थमिमं भृशम् ।\nशुश्रावार्तस्वरं घोरमथ मुक्तं स्त्रिया तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Indra went to Mount Manasa and, meditating hard on this matter, then heard a woman's terrible cry of distress.\""}},{"n":7,"text":"अभिधावतु मा कश्चित्पुरुषस्त्रातु चैव ह ।\nपतिं च मे प्रदिशतु स्वयं वा पतिरस्तु मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"She cried: 'Let some man run here and save me! Let him give me a husband, or himself be my husband!'\""}},{"n":8,"text":"पुरंदरस्तु तामाह मा भैर्नास्ति भयं तव ।\nएवमुक्त्वा ततोऽपश्यत्केशिनं स्थितमग्रतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Indra said to her, 'Do not fear; you have nothing to be afraid of.' Having said that, he saw the demon Keshin standing before him.\""}},{"n":9,"text":"किरीटिनं गदापाणिं धातुमन्तमिवाचलम् ।\nहस्ते गृहीत्वा तां कन्यामथैनं वासवोऽब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Keshin wore a crown and held a mace in hand, like a mountain rich in minerals. Taking that girl by the hand, Vasava then said to him...\""}},{"n":10,"text":"अनार्यकर्मन्कस्मात्त्वमिमां कन्यां जिहीर्षसि ।\nवज्रिणं मां विजानीहि विरमास्याः प्रबाधनात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'Ignoble deed-doer, why do you want to carry off this girl? Know me as the wielder of the thunderbolt, and stop tormenting her.'\""}},{"text":"केश्युवाच","meaning":{"en":"Keshin said:"}},{"n":11,"text":"विसृजस्व त्वमेवैनां शक्रैषा प्रार्थिता मया ।\nक्षमं ते जीवतो गन्तुं स्वपुरं पाकशासन ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'You yourself must let her go, Shakra; I desire her. It is wise for you to go back to your city alive, Indra.'\""}},{"text":"मार्कण्डेय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Markandeya said:"}},{"n":12,"text":"एवमुक्त्वा गदां केशी चिक्षेपेन्द्रवधाय वै ।\nतामापतन्तीं चिच्छेद मध्ये वज्रेण वासवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Having said this, Keshin hurled his mace to kill Indra, but Vasava cut it in mid-air with his thunderbolt as it came.\""}},{"n":13,"text":"अथास्य शैलशिखरं केशी क्रुद्धो व्यवासृजत् ।\nतदापतन्तं संप्रेक्ष्य शैलशृङ्गं शतक्रतुः ।\nबिभेद राजन्वज्रेण भुवि तन्निपपात ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Then, angry, Keshin hurled a mountain peak at him. Seeing the peak falling, Indra, the hundred-sacrifice lord, broke it with his thunderbolt, king, and it fell to the earth.\""}},{"n":14,"text":"पतता तु तदा केशी तेन शृङ्गेण ताडितः ।\nहित्वा कन्यां महाभागां प्राद्रवद्भृशपीडितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"As it fell, Keshin was struck by that peak. Leaving the fortunate girl, he fled, badly hurt.\""}},{"n":15,"text":"अपयातेऽसुरे तस्मिंस्तां कन्यां वासवोऽब्रवीत् ।\nकासि कस्यासि किं चेह कुरुषे त्वं शुभानने ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"When the asura was gone, Vasava asked the girl: 'Who are you, whose daughter are you, and what do you do here, fair-faced one?'\""}},{"text":"कन्योवाच","meaning":{"en":"The girl said:"}},{"n":16,"text":"अहं प्रजापतेः कन्या देवसेनेति विश्रुता ।\nभगिनी दैत्यसेना मे सा पूर्वं केशिना हृता ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'I am Prajapati's daughter, known as Devasena. My sister Daityasena was carried off by Keshin earlier.'\""}},{"n":17,"text":"सहैवावां भगिन्यौ तु सखीभिः सह मानसम् ।\nआगच्छावेह रत्यर्थमनुज्ञाप्य प्रजापतिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'We two sisters used to come to Mount Manasa together with our friends, after taking Prajapati's leave, to amuse ourselves.'\""}},{"n":18,"text":"नित्यं चावां प्रार्थयते हर्तुं केशी महासुरः ।\nइच्छत्येनं दैत्यसेना न त्वहं पाकशासन ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'The great asura Keshin always wanted to carry us off. Daityasena likes him; I do not, Indra.'\""}},{"n":19,"text":"सा हृता तेन भगवन्मुक्ताहं त्वद्बलेन तु ।\nत्वया देवेन्द्र निर्दिष्टं पतिमिच्छामि दुर्जयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'She was taken by him, lord, but I was freed by your strength. O king of the gods, I want a husband whom you will name, one hard to defeat.'\""}},{"text":"इन्द्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Indra said:"}},{"n":20,"text":"मम मातृष्वसेया त्वं माता दाक्षायणी मम ।\nआख्यातं त्वहमिच्छामि स्वयमात्मबलं त्वया ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'You are my cousin, the daughter of my mother's sister; my mother is Daksha's daughter. I want you to tell me yourself about your own strength.'\""}},{"text":"कन्योवाच","meaning":{"en":"The girl said:"}},{"n":21,"text":"अबलाहं महाबाहो पतिस्तु बलवान्मम ।\nवरदानात्पितुर्भावी सुरासुरनमस्कृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'I am weak, mighty-armed one, but my husband will be strong. By my father's boon he will be saluted by gods and asuras.'\""}},{"text":"इन्द्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Indra said:"}},{"n":22,"text":"कीदृशं वै बलं देवि पत्युस्तव भविष्यति ।\nएतदिच्छाम्यहं श्रोतुं तव वाक्यमनिन्दिते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'What kind of strength will your husband have, goddess? I want to hear it from you, blameless one.'\""}},{"text":"कन्योवाच","meaning":{"en":"The girl said:"}},{"n":23,"text":"देवदानवयक्षाणां किंनरोरगरक्षसाम् ।\nजेता स दृष्टो दुष्टानां महावीर्यो महाबलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'One who conquers gods, danavas, yakshas, kinnaras, serpents and rakshasas, and wicked beings, a man of great valor and strength, has been foretold.'\""}},{"n":24,"text":"यस्तु सर्वाणि भूतानि त्वया सह विजेष्यति ।\nस हि मे भविता भर्ता ब्रह्मण्यः कीर्तिवर्धनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'The one who will conquer all beings along with you will be my husband, devoted to brahmins and increasing fame.'\""}},{"text":"मार्कण्डेय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Markandeya said:"}},{"n":25,"text":"इन्द्रस्तस्या वचः श्रुत्वा दुःखितोऽचिन्तयद्भृशम् ।\nअस्या देव्याः पतिर्नास्ति यादृशं संप्रभाषते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Hearing her words, Indra was troubled and thought deeply: 'This goddess has no husband such as she describes.'\""}},{"n":26,"text":"अथापश्यत्स उदये भास्करं भास्करद्युतिः ।\nसोमं चैव महाभागं विशमानं दिवाकरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Then Indra, radiant as the sun, saw the sun at its rising and the greatly fortunate Moon entering the sun.\""}},{"n":27,"text":"अमावास्यां संप्रवृत्तं मुहूर्तं रौद्रमेव च ।\nदेवासुरं च संग्रामं सोऽपश्यदुदये गिरौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"He saw that the new moon had come, a fierce moment, and at the rising mountain he saw the battle of gods and asuras.\""}},{"n":28,"text":"लोहितैश्च घनैर्युक्तां पूर्वां संध्यां शतक्रतुः ।\nअपश्यल्लोहितोदं च भगवान्वरुणालयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The hundred-sacrifice lord saw the eastern twilight bound with red clouds, and the blessed ocean, abode of Varuna, with red water.\""}},{"n":29,"text":"भृगुभिश्चाङ्गिरोभिश्च हुतं मन्त्रैः पृथग्विधैः ।\nहव्यं गृहीत्वा वह्निं च प्रविशन्तं दिवाकरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"He saw the fire entering the sun, carrying the offering poured with various mantras by the Bhrigus and Angirases.\""}},{"n":30,"text":"पर्व चैव चतुर्विंशं तदा सूर्यमुपस्थितम् ।\nतथा धर्मगतं रौद्रं सोमं सूर्यगतं च तम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The twenty-fourth lunar day had come to the sun, and the fierce Moon, fixed in dharma, was in the sun.\""}},{"n":31,"text":"समालोक्यैकतामेव शशिनो भास्करस्य च ।\nसमवायं तु तं रौद्रं दृष्ट्वा शक्रो व्यचिन्तयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Seeing the moon and sun as one, Indra thought about that terrible conjunction.\""}},{"n":32,"text":"एष रौद्रश्च संघातो महान्युक्तश्च तेजसा ।\nसोमस्य वह्निसूर्याभ्यामद्भुतोऽयं समागमः ।\nजनयेद्यं सुतं सोमः सोऽस्या देव्याः पतिर्भवेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'This terrible, great meeting is joined with power: the Moon with fire and the sun, a wondrous union. The son whom Soma begets will be this goddess's husband.'\""}},{"n":33,"text":"अग्निश्चैतैर्गुणैर्युक्तः सर्वैरग्निश्च देवता ।\nएष चेज्जनयेद्गर्भं सोऽस्या देव्याः पतिर्भवेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'Fire has all these qualities, and fire is a god too. If he begets a child, that child will be this goddess's husband.'\""}},{"n":34,"text":"एवं संचिन्त्य भगवान्ब्रह्मलोकं तदा गतः ।\nगृहीत्वा देवसेनां तामवन्दत्स पितामहम् ।\nउवाच चास्या देव्यास्त्वं साधु शूरं पतिं दिश ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Thinking so, the blessed Indra went to Brahma's world, took Devasena, and saluted the Grandfather. He said: 'Give this goddess a good, heroic husband.'\""}},{"text":"ब्रह्मोवाच","meaning":{"en":"Brahma said:"}},{"n":35,"text":"यथैतच्चिन्तितं कार्यं त्वया दानवसूदन ।\nतथा स भविता गर्भो बलवानुरुविक्रमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'Slayer of danavas, as you have thought it out, so will the child be, strong and of vast might.'\""}},{"n":36,"text":"स भविष्यति सेनानीस्त्वया सह शतक्रतो ।\nअस्या देव्याः पतिश्चैव स भविष्यति वीर्यवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'He will be your commander, hundred-sacrifice lord, and the valiant husband of this goddess.'\""}},{"text":"मार्कण्डेय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Markandeya said:"}},{"n":37,"text":"एतच्छ्रुत्वा नमस्तस्मै कृत्वासौ सह कन्यया ।\nतत्राभ्यगच्छद्देवेन्द्रो यत्र देवर्षयोऽभवन् ।\nवसिष्ठप्रमुखा मुख्या विप्रेन्द्राः सुमहाव्रताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Hearing this and bowing to him, Indra, king of the gods, went with the girl to where the divine sages were, chief among them Vasishtha, lords of brahmins of great vows.\""}},{"n":38,"text":"भागार्थं तपसोपात्तं तेषां सोमं तथाध्वरे ।\nपिपासवो ययुर्देवाः शतक्रतुपुरोगमाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The gods, led by Indra, went there thirsting for the Soma set aside for their share at that sacrifice, obtained by the sages' austerity.\""}},{"n":39,"text":"इष्टिं कृत्वा यथान्यायं सुसमिद्धे हुताशने ।\nजुहुवुस्ते महात्मानो हव्यं सर्वदिवौकसाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Having duly performed the rite in the well-kindled fire, those great ones offered the oblation for all the dwellers of heaven.\""}},{"n":40,"text":"समाहूतो हुतवहः सोऽद्भुतः सूर्यमण्डलात् ।\nविनिःसृत्याययौ वह्निर्वाग्यतो विधिवत्प्रभुः ।\nआगम्याहवनीयं वै तैर्द्विजैर्मन्त्रतो हुतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The wondrous fire, summoned, came forth from the sun's disk, silent, as the rule required, the lord. Arriving at the offering fire, he received the oblation poured by those brahmins with mantras.\""}},{"n":41,"text":"स तत्र विविधं हव्यं प्रतिगृह्य हुताशनः ।\nऋषिभ्यो भरतश्रेष्ठ प्रायच्छत दिवौकसाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"There the fire received the various offerings and gave them to the sages and the dwellers of heaven, best of the Bharatas.\""}},{"n":42,"text":"निष्क्रामंश्चाप्यपश्यत्स पत्नीस्तेषां महात्मनाम् ।\nस्वेष्वाश्रमेषूपविष्टाः स्नायन्तीश्च यथासुखम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"As he went out he saw the wives of those great sages, seated at ease in their hermitages and bathing.\""}},{"n":43,"text":"रुक्मवेदिनिभास्तास्तु चन्द्रलेखा इवामलाः ।\nहुताशनार्चिप्रतिमाः सर्वास्तारा इवाद्भुताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"They were like golden altars, spotless as crescent moons, like flames of fire, all wondrous as stars.\""}},{"n":44,"text":"स तद्गतेन मनसा बभूव क्षुभितेन्द्रियः ।\nपत्नीर्दृष्ट्वा द्विजेन्द्राणां वह्निः कामवशं ययौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"With his mind fixed on them, his senses were stirred. Seeing the wives of the best of brahmins, the fire fell under the power of desire.\""}},{"n":45,"text":"स भूयश्चिन्तयामास न न्याय्यं क्षुभितोऽस्मि यत् ।\nसाध्वीः पत्नीर्द्विजेन्द्राणामकामाः कामयाम्यहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"He thought again: 'It is not right that I am stirred. I desire the virtuous wives of the best brahmins, who do not desire me.'\""}},{"n":46,"text":"नैताः शक्या मया द्रष्टुं स्प्रष्टुं वाप्यनिमित्ततः ।\nगार्हपत्यं समाविश्य तस्मात्पश्याम्यभीक्ष्णशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'I cannot look at them or touch them without cause. So I will enter the household fire and see them again and again.'\""}},{"n":47,"text":"संस्पृशन्निव सर्वास्ताः शिखाभिः काञ्चनप्रभाः ।\nपश्यमानश्च मुमुदे गार्हपत्यं समाश्रितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"He seemed to touch them all with his flames, golden in radiance, and he rejoiced, looking at them, settled in the household fire.\""}},{"n":48,"text":"निरुष्य तत्र सुचिरमेवं वह्निर्वशं गतः ।\nमनस्तासु विनिक्षिप्य कामयानो वराङ्गनाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Dwelling there a long time, the fire fell into the power of desire, setting his mind upon those lovely women.\""}},{"n":49,"text":"कामसंतप्तहृदयो देहत्यागे सुनिश्चितः ।\nअलाभे ब्राह्मणस्त्रीणामग्निर्वनमुपागतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"His heart burning with love, firmly resolved to give up his body since he could not win the brahmins' wives, Agni went into the forest.\""}},{"n":50,"text":"स्वाहा तं दक्षदुहिता प्रथमं कामयत्तदा ।\nसा तस्य छिद्रमन्वैच्छच्चिरात्प्रभृति भामिनी ।\nअप्रमत्तस्य देवस्य न चापश्यदनिन्दिता ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Svaha, Daksha's daughter, had loved him from the first. For a long time that fair woman had looked for an opening with the ever-watchful god, and she, blameless, did not find one.\""}},{"n":51,"text":"सा तं ज्ञात्वा यथावत्तु वह्निं वनमुपागतम् ।\nतत्त्वतः कामसंतप्तं चिन्तयामास भामिनी ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"She learned that the fire had gone into the forest, truly burning with desire, and the lovely woman thought it over.\""}},{"n":52,"text":"अहं सप्तर्षिपत्नीनां कृत्वा रूपाणि पावकम् ।\nकामयिष्यामि कामार्तं तासां रूपेण मोहितम् ।\nएवं कृते प्रीतिरस्य कामावाप्तिश्च मे भवेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'I will take the forms of the seven sages' wives and make love to the fire, who is tormented by desire and deluded by their appearance. If I do this, he will be pleased and I will get my wish.'\""}}]}]}